       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. SPECIALNAMES.
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SOURCE-COMPUTER. X86-64.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER. X86-64
           PROGRAM COLLATING SEQUENCE IS REVERSED.
       SPECIAL-NAMES.
           SWITCH-1 IS SW1 ON STATUS IS SW1-ON OFF STATUS IS SW1-OFF
           ALPHABET REVERSED IS "Z" THRU "A"
           ALPHABET PLAIN IS NATIVE
           CLASS HEX-DIGIT IS "0" THRU "9" "A" THRU "F"
           CURRENCY SIGN IS "E"
           DECIMAL-POINT IS COMMA.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 PRICE   PIC 9(4)V99 VALUE 1234,5.
       01 EDITED  PIC EEE.EE9,99.
       01 HEXVAL  PIC X(4) VALUE "1F0A".
       01 NOTHEX  PIC X(4) VALUE "12G4".
       01 LOW-ONE PIC X VALUE LOW-VALUE.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN-PARA.
           MOVE PRICE TO EDITED.
           DISPLAY "[" EDITED "]".
           IF HEXVAL HEX-DIGIT DISPLAY "HEX OK".
           IF NOTHEX IS NOT HEX-DIGIT DISPLAY "NOT HEX OK".
           IF SW1-OFF DISPLAY "SWITCH OFF".
           IF NOT SW1-ON DISPLAY "SWITCH NOT ON".
           IF "A" > "B" DISPLAY "REVERSED ORDER".
           IF LOW-ONE = "Z" DISPLAY "LOW-VALUE IS Z".
           DISPLAY "NO " WITH NO ADVANCING.
           DISPLAY "ADVANCING" UPON SW1.
           STOP RUN.
